% Test cases for the spinal orthosis policy (spinal_orthoses.le): synthetic
% claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33790 and per payment condition of
% Policy Article A52500, each stating only what its record shows. Several
% codes are on the face-to-face and prior authorization lists: a payable
% claim for one of them has the encounter, the order before delivery and the
% affirmed prior authorization in its record. The queries: whether the claim
% is payable (the first query, so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it
% is reasonable and necessary, and what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base spinal_orthoses cases includes these resources:
    spinal_orthoses.

the knowledge base spinal_orthoses cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete file for a custom fitted LSO (L0637) after lumbar spine
% surgery: the indication in the record, the supplier's record of the
% modifications made at the fitting, the face-to-face encounter, the order
% before delivery and the prior authorization (L0637 is on both lists).
scenario lso_after_surgery_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the LSO.
    the HCPCS code of the LSO is "L0637".
    the LSO is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    the medical record of Ann documents spinal surgery.
    the records of the supplier justify the modifications made at the fitting of the LSO.
    the treating practitioner examined Ann for the LSO in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-02-01.
    the order for the LSO is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the LSO is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the LSO includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the LSO includes order date.
    the order for the LSO includes description of the item.
    the order for the LSO includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the LSO includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the LSO was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    prior authorization for the LSO was affirmed on 2026-03-01.
    the LSO was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the LSO.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The same file without the supplier's record of the modifications made at
% the fitting: reasonable and necessary, but the code selected is not
% justified.
scenario lso_no_fitting_record is:
    claim 1 is for the LSO.
    the HCPCS code of the LSO is "L0637".
    the LSO is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    the medical record of Ann documents spinal surgery.
    the treating practitioner examined Ann for the LSO in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-02-01.
    the order for the LSO is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the LSO is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the LSO includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the LSO includes order date.
    the order for the LSO includes description of the item.
    the order for the LSO includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the LSO includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the LSO was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    prior authorization for the LSO was affirmed on 2026-03-01.
    the LSO was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the LSO.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the records of the supplier justify the modifications made at the fitting of the LSO"]].

% The same file without the prior authorization: the dated fact the prior
% authorization list requires is missing.
scenario lso_no_prior_authorization is:
    claim 1 is for the LSO.
    the HCPCS code of the LSO is "L0637".
    the LSO is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    the medical record of Ann documents spinal surgery.
    the records of the supplier justify the modifications made at the fitting of the LSO.
    the treating practitioner examined Ann for the LSO in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-02-01.
    the order for the LSO is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the LSO is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the LSO includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the LSO includes order date.
    the order for the LSO includes description of the item.
    the order for the LSO includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the LSO includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the LSO was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    the LSO was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the LSO.
    pay expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].

% Off-the-shelf orthoses for two indications: an LSO (L0650) supporting weak
% spinal muscles, a TLSO (L0457) after a vertebral fracture (a spinal
% injury). Neither needs a reason for custom fabrication.
scenario off_the_shelf_indications is:
    claim 1 is for the LSO.
    the HCPCS code of the LSO is "L0650".
    the LSO is furnished to Ben.
    the medical record of Ben documents weak spinal muscles.
    claim 2 is for the TLSO.
    the HCPCS code of the TLSO is "L0457".
    the TLSO is furnished to Cy.
    the medical record of Cy documents spinal injury.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% An LSO (L0650) for a beneficiary whose record documents obesity and no
% indication of the LCD: not reasonable and necessary.
scenario no_indication is:
    claim 1 is for the LSO.
    the HCPCS code of the LSO is "L0650".
    the LSO is furnished to Dee.
    the medical record of Dee documents obesity.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% A custom fabricated TLSO (L0486) for a spinal deformity the treating
% practitioner finds a prefabricated orthosis cannot fit; the same orthosis
% for a beneficiary about whom nobody has recorded that finding (a judgment
% needed).
scenario custom_fabricated is:
    claim 1 is for the body jacket.
    the HCPCS code of the body jacket is "L0486".
    the body jacket is furnished to Eve.
    the medical record of Eve documents spinal deformity.
    the finding custom fabrication required about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the kyphoscoliosis cannot be accommodated by a prefabricated TLSO".
    claim 2 is for the other body jacket.
    the HCPCS code of the other body jacket is "L0486".
    the other body jacket is furnished to Fay.
    the medical record of Fay documents spinal deformity.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding custom fabrication required about Fay is established"].

% A protective body sock (L0984): not a brace, in no benefit, never payable.
scenario body_sock is:
    claim 1 is for the body sock.
    the HCPCS code of the body sock is "L0984".
    the body sock is furnished to Gus.
    the medical record of Gus documents spinal surgery.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].

% The Council finds the record does not show why a prefabricated TLSO would
% not do: the custom fabricated orthosis is not reasonable and necessary.
scenario council_custom_fabrication_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the body jacket.
    the HCPCS code of the body jacket is "L0486".
    the body jacket is furnished to Hal.
    the medical record of Hal documents pain requiring restricted trunk mobility.
    the finding custom fabrication required about Hal is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the treating practitioner's notes order a custom jacket but describe no trunk shape or size a prefabricated orthosis could not fit".
    rn expects answers [].
